From: gloat <4354076+gloat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:54:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] layout: fill-single-column, a lone column fills the view

New layout flag. While a column is the only one in its scrolling space it
is shown full-width; with two or more, each column uses its own width.
The first window on an empty workspace gets a full-width initial
configure, so it opens at that size instead of resizing after mapping.

Columns keep an is_only_column flag that add_column and
remove_column_by_idx update (every column insert and removal goes through
them), checked in verify_invariants. The stored width is unchanged, so
Mod+R on a lone column takes effect once a second column joins.
